findings.body:
The lookup fires on **every** webhook mismatch — including public and unknown-visibility repos — but on those the result can never change the outcome: the override below requires `_is_private_or_internal_visibility`, and lookup failures fail-closed on non-private. So denied public-repo PRs (exactly the spam path this gate exists to keep free) each spend one GitHub API call, contradicting `README.md:246` ("a denied gate costs **zero API calls**") and the new `docs/SECURITY.md` text that scopes the lookup to "private/internal". Guard by visibility so the cheapest-first contract holds and docs match code:

```suggestion
    if _is_private_or_internal_visibility(
        repo_visibility
    ) and _author_gate_needs_permission_lookup(
        gate=author_gate_raw,
        webhook_association=pr_author_association,
    ):
```
